  "_comment": "Recipes of the four Stone Age stages (ADR 0059), loaded after recipes.json with the same schema. New in-world types, each listing every unit it uses in `ingredients` (the browser shows them as a row) and `hours` in game hours of the calendar (sleeping counts): bury = an earth oven: dig a pit with a shovel (right click soil or sand), lay the ingredients in, cover them with `cover_count` of `cover`, lay `fuel_count` of `fuel` on top and light it; after `hours` an empty hand digs out the output. rack = hang `input` on a drying rack: mode dry takes `hours`; mode smoke needs a lit firepit right beside or under the rack. stroke = work on a surface (`on`: ground = any top face, stone = natural rock, sandstone, loom = a placed loom) with right clicks of `tool`: lay the first ingredient on it (a picker chooses when several recipes start with it), add the rest, then `strokes` right clicks with the tool; `grit` must be added every `grit_every` strokes and `water` means a water source within a block. soak = lay the ingredients in water (right click the water with the first); after `hours` they are done. trap = set the item in water; every `every_hours` it catches the output with `chance` (flowing water doubles it when `river` is set).",
